    "review": "The hero remained alive at full health when the planner stopped. Four accepted thief interceptions had already spent the floor-wide species chase allowance (decisions 2290, 2293–2295; lines 6720, 6728, 6731, 6734). The last accepted melee at decision 2755, line 8062, left a visible thief two cells away with the staff empty. Decision 2756, line 8063, then exhausted. An identified deep-sleep stone was carried, but the thief controller stopped before disabling utility; ordinary sleep use also required low health. A reduced public-input regression reproduces this exclusion. The proposed correction retains a known targeted sleep throw for a lone visible thief after attacks and the chase allowance are exhausted, without extending pursuit or crediting a defeat. Original-source tests fail the two expected selection assertions; the candidate passes all five new tests and the full 1902-test suite, with four skips. Isolated helper probes match the preceding two recorded melee selections, but do not reconstruct all original runtime memory. Selecting sleep does not establish successful application, subsequent progress or survival.",
    "learnings": "Exhausted pursuit does not mean every useful action is exhausted. Check known single-target disabling resources before a species-specific terminal veto, retaining visibility, clear-shot, eligibility and cooldown checks. Do not reset chase budgets or infer sleep, defeat or collection from a selected throw."
